      "findings": [
        "The compiler-matched spec permits row/col-major A and B and lists BMG G21/G31 BF16 A/B, FP32 accumulator/result, M<=8,N=16,K=16: the candidate's QK combination.",
        "Installed headers map col_major to SPIR-V ColumnMajor and forward layout/stride. The generic load accepts local-space pointers; actual IGC local-load transformation is unknown.",
        "BMG limits: stride*sizeof(T) multiple of 8 and <=2^24; base 4-byte aligned. Candidate stride=256 BF16=512 bytes; alignas(4) tile bases move by 16-cell/16-dimension multiples.",
        "matrix_available checks subgroup 16, BF16/BF16/FP32/FP32 dimensions 8x16x16, and local-memory capacity; query has no layout field.",
        "No IGC source, target JIT, emitted IR/ISA, SLM transactions, bank metric, or performance was inspected. IGC may rearrange or canonicalize the requested layout.",
        "Intel LLVM issue #22926 reports BMG-G31 matrix-query failure on DPC++ 2025.3.3/runtime 26.05; Intel response calls that compiler old. Version-mismatched counterevidence, not a finding about installed v7.1.0-pre/IGC 2.41.5."
      ],
